<!-- TECHNOPERA 2024 — English only (source: Gdańsk Shakespeare Theatre event page) -->
<section class="edition-2024" id="technopera-2024">
  <div class="container content">
    <h2 class="section-title">{technopera2024Title}</h2>
    <p class="edition-2024-subtitle">What the machine does not reveal to us, and why?</p>
    <p class="edition-2024-meta">Gdańsk Shakespeare Theatre · Gdańsk · 6.12.2024 · 20:00 · 1h15</p>

    <div class="edition-2024-body">
      <p>Technopera is a multimedia event combining opera with techno culture, referring to projects of the cult Tricity art group C.U.K.T. from the late 1990s. This futuristic spectacle is built from fragments of popular-science and science-fiction films arranged as a dialogue between characters. Libretto by Podletz (Artur Kozdrowski) and Peter Style (Piotr Wyrzykowski); music by Michał Jacaszek and NeoQuartet; cast: actor Mikołaj Robert Jurkowski, soprano and performer Aleksandra Klimczak, and the Alien, the Machine and the Cyborg generated with artificial intelligence — with the libretto, played live by a VJ, as the choreographic and dramaturgical reference for actors and musicians. The first Technopera took place in 1996; this continuation is a collaboration of C.U.K.T. with NeoQuartet and Jacaszek. The motto of Technopera 2024 is the question “What does the machine not reveal to us, and why?”</p>
    </div>

    <p class="edition-2024-source">
      Source:
      <a href={TECHNOPERA_2024_SOURCE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gdańsk Shakespeare Theatre event page</a>
